Fixed.

**Bug:** `src/import_merge.ts:7` compared URLs with `b.url === inc.url`, a case-sensitive string compare. Since hostnames are case-insensitive, `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` and `https://example.com/a` weren't recognized as the same URL, so the incoming bookmark was added as a duplicate entry.

**Fix:** Added a `sameUrl` helper that parses both URLs with `new URL(...)` and compares the normalized `host` (which lowercases the hostname) plus `pathname`. Unparseable URLs fall back to a raw `===` compare. `mergeImports` now uses `sameUrl` for the duplicate check.

**Verified:** `deno test` — 5 passed, 0 failed. Added two regression tests: hostname-case merge (the reported bug) and a no-match append (guards against over-merging).


